WEBVTT

00:00.400 --> 00:04.455
Welcome to the Two Rivers Future Ready Skills Academy.

00:04.505 --> 00:13.577
It links 13 Western Australian schools, from Foundation to Year 12, with emerging technology, industry and real careers.

00:13.627 --> 00:18.594
Everything in this tour uses sample data, so feel free to explore.

00:22.453 --> 00:26.880
At the heart of the Academy are the five Future Ready Skills.

00:26.930 --> 00:32.825
The framework shows how each skill grows, year by year, right through to Year 12.

00:37.566 --> 00:42.083
Resources brings together everything from the Future Ready Skills website:

00:42.133 --> 00:47.268
class presentations for every year band, posters, games, lessons and staff learning.

00:49.518 --> 00:52.286
Teachers start with Plan a report.

00:52.336 --> 00:58.421
Tell the Academy what your students will learn about, choose a year level,

00:58.471 --> 01:01.985
and describe what they'll do in the lesson.

01:02.035 --> 01:12.762
Then say how many lessons you have, and how long each one is. The Academy shows the lesson delivery time, a school-based estimate.

01:12.812 --> 01:20.802
Then open the learning areas and tick the WA Curriculum strands, or go deeper to the sub-strands.

01:20.852 --> 01:31.496
The Academy suggests learning intentions from your answers. They're short to choose here, and written out in full in your report.

01:31.546 --> 01:37.216
Finally, choose the Future Ready Skills you want students to develop.

01:47.963 --> 01:53.392
Three new switches shape the report around your class.

01:53.442 --> 02:05.059
Differentiation sets three quest levels. Your school can name them, and they start as Hero, Legendary and Immortal.

02:05.109 --> 02:14.697
Explicit Teaching is only for core concepts, key vocabulary and numeracy, not the whole lesson.

02:14.747 --> 02:26.161
And the Student AI Use Guide sets the AI rules for the task. For Year 5, that's no AI or a teacher demonstration.

02:30.422 --> 02:34.759
In seconds you have a learning plan written for your year level:

02:34.809 --> 02:40.037
curriculum links for every lesson, a lesson sequence with 'I can' statements,

02:40.087 --> 02:43.808
and experts, partners and events that match your topic.

02:43.858 --> 02:49.634
With the switches on, you also get differentiated quests, explicit teaching segments,

02:49.684 --> 02:56.078
and the AI rules for the task, with a classroom poster and a student acknowledgement to print.

03:16.161 --> 03:21.357
One click turns the plan into a slide deck in your school's colours,

03:21.407 --> 03:24.751
ready to present, or download as PowerPoint.

03:24.801 --> 03:30.614
Students see the AI rules first, then choose their quest at the right level.

03:30.664 --> 03:37.865
Or switch the style to an EDI segments deck: I do, we do, you do, for the key ideas and words.

03:46.896 --> 03:49.671
Every plan now fits your lessons.

03:49.721 --> 03:55.320
Press Lesson script for one timed page per lesson, ready to print.

03:55.370 --> 03:59.686
Keep the standard script, or have Claude write one.

04:03.843 --> 04:08.034
My profile shows your FRS Lesson Time:

04:08.084 --> 04:19.082
time logged in, plus lesson delivery time, a school-based estimate, by activity and AITSL Standard.

04:19.132 --> 04:22.988
Certificates arrive every 50 hours.

04:23.938 --> 04:27.252
Lead teachers mentor new FRS teachers.

04:27.302 --> 04:35.928
Teachers at my school shows everyone's hours and the FRS Trained flag, which emails a certificate.

04:35.978 --> 04:46.375
Invite a teacher picks a session, date and place, and the Academy sends the email, a reminder and a reflection prompt.

04:53.572 --> 04:57.750
If you just want the Future Ready Skills, turn on FRS content only.

04:57.800 --> 05:00.022
Choose a year level and your skills,

05:00.072 --> 05:08.289
and you get the progressions, student 'I can' statements, class presentations, posters and lesson resources, all ready to download.

05:17.510 --> 05:21.592
School Leaders see how their school is using the Academy:

05:21.642 --> 05:28.334
teachers, reports, the skills in focus, and student survey results, with printable summaries,

05:28.384 --> 05:31.089
and how many teachers are FRS Trained.

05:35.771 --> 05:41.208
Leaders, Lead teachers and Career Practitioners also keep the school's contacts here,

05:41.258 --> 05:44.241
and can import a whole list from a spreadsheet.

05:47.938 --> 05:53.926
Industry partners and experts offer guest talks, site visits and volunteers,

05:53.976 --> 05:57.897
and answer teachers' requests through the Academy.

06:00.187 --> 06:03.461
The Academy team manages approvals, events and schools,

06:03.511 --> 06:06.302
tracks every professional learning certificate,

06:06.352 --> 06:10.895
and measures the impact of the Future Ready Skills across the whole network.

06:21.871 --> 06:27.709
Now it's your turn. Use Try as at the top to explore each role,

06:27.759 --> 06:33.876
then please take our six-minute survey and tell us what you think.
